<!--
  Chapter 20 — Microservice Anti-Patterns: detect them from evidence, and keep them out.
    model/    a plain-text architecture model (services, calls per request, tables, libraries,
              deploy history) and its parser
    detect/   detectors for distributed monolith (lockstep deploys), deep chains, cycles, chatty
              calls, fan-out, nano-services, shared databases, shared domain libraries, version skew;
              a report; a baseline that only shrinks
    chatty/   Monte Carlo: N+1 sequential vs parallel vs batch vs local replica
  resources/architecture/ holds FoodFleet's 2023 and 2024 models and the accepted-findings baseline.
  Plain Java; Spring Boot's test starter only for JUnit and AssertJ.
-->
